{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the hair in the affliction has turned white.</b> Any white hair is a sign of weakness in the body, and the whitening of a person's hair in old age proves it. So too, all white horses are feeble in strength, and likewise any white sheep is not as good as the color of other kinds of hair, for every white appearance originates from the white moisture that brings about laziness, for the activity of every lazy person is neither with force nor with strength."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:36:09.640886914Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}